1. Scope and acceptance

This license applies to the copyright holder's software, documentation, and
other materials expressly distributed under this license (the "Software").
It applies only to rights that the copyright holder is entitled to license.
Exercising rights granted by this license constitutes acceptance of its terms.
This is a source-available academic license, not an OSI-approved open-source
license. The identifier above is a project-specific LicenseRef.

2. Eligible users and permitted purposes

An "Eligible User" is a student, educator, or researcher acting solely in that
capacity at a nonprofit educational institution, nonprofit research institution,
or public research institution, for that institution's non-commercial academic
research or teaching. Employees, agents, and contractors acting for a for-profit
entity are not Eligible Users for that activity, even if they also hold an
academic affiliation or intend to publish their results.

"Permitted Purposes" means non-commercial academic research, teaching, study,
and reproducibility of scholarly results by Eligible Users. Ordinary tuition
and public or charitable research funding do not alone make an otherwise
eligible activity commercial. A nonprofit affiliation alone does not make a
commercial activity permissible.

3. Limited, royalty-free grant

Subject to all terms below, the copyright holder grants Eligible Users a
worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-sublicensable license to access,
copy, install, compile, execute, inspect, and modify the Software solely for
Permitted Purposes. No commercial-use right is granted. All other rights are
reserved. Commercial use requires a separate written commercial license from
the relevant copyright holder and payment of the fees agreed in that license
before use begins. Other excluded uses require separate written permission.
These terms do not promise that a separate license will be offered.

4. Commercial and other excluded uses

Under this academic license, you may not use, modify, distribute, or make the Software available, directly
or indirectly, for commercial advantage, monetary compensation, or the benefit
of a for-profit business. Prohibited activities include:

(a) corporate internal research, evaluation, product development, or production;
(b) paid consulting, contract research, or services for a commercial client;
(c) industry-sponsored research carried out for a sponsor's business benefit,
    including projects granting a commercial sponsor privileged exploitation
    rights or exclusive access to results;
(d) commercial hosted services, APIs, software-as-a-service, or paid access;
(e) incorporation into commercial software, products, workflows, or services;
(f) using the Software to train, fine-tune, distill, or generate models,
    checkpoints, datasets, or other assets for commercial exploitation; and
(g) evasion of these restrictions through affiliates, academic collaborators,
    intermediaries, wrappers, or modifications.

Free-of-charge access, publication of results, or describing work as "research"
does not by itself make an excluded use permissible.

5. Redistribution, modifications, and notices

You may share copies or modifications only for Permitted Purposes, with these
terms, all copyright notices, and all applicable third-party notices intact.
Recipients must obtain their license directly under these terms; you may not
grant broader rights, remove the non-commercial restriction, or relicense the
copyright holder's Software. Clearly identify your modifications and do not
misrepresent them as an official release. Public source forks may be hosted
with these terms prominently included; execution and other licensed uses
remain limited to Eligible Users and Permitted Purposes. Rights independently
granted by a hosting platform's applicable terms are not withdrawn here.

6. Scholarly publication and outputs

Eligible Users may publish scholarly papers, factual findings, and benchmark
results from Permitted Purposes, including in journals that charge publication
or subscription fees. Acknowledge FSCETP and the version used. This license
does not claim ownership of your independently created findings or data.
The grant does not authorize operating the Software to produce assets for
commercial exploitation, or distributing Software or derivative code inside
an output under less restrictive terms. Independently applicable rights in
data, models, and third-party materials must be respected.

